  "body": "Fixes #3278\n\n## Description\n\nAdd a `disableKnowledgeContext()` Builder method to `HarnessAgent` that precisely disables knowledge-related system prompt injection without affecting AGENTS.md, MEMORY.md, or memory tools.\n\nCurrently the only way to disable knowledge injection is `disableWorkspaceContext()`, which is a nuclear option — it disables everything including AGENTS.md, MEMORY.md, and session context. This PR adds a granular switch for agents that use a custom enterprise knowledge tool (e.g. Solr + Milvus + Rerank) instead of the framework's local `knowledge/` directory.\n\n## Changes\n\n### HarnessAgent.java\n- Add `disableKnowledgeContext` boolean flag to Builder (default `false`)\n- Add `disableKnowledgeContext()` Builder method with Javadoc\n- Pass flag to `WorkspaceContextMiddleware` via new 7-arg constructor\n\n### WorkspaceContextMiddleware.java\n- Add 2 new `WORKSPACE_FILES_NOTICE_NO_KNOWLEDGE_*` constants (omit `knowledge/KNOWLEDGE.md` mention)\n- Add `disableKnowledgeContext` field\n- Add 7-arg constructor; existing constructors delegate with `false` (backward compatible)\n- **IO short-circuit**: skip `readKnowledgeMd()` entirely when disabled\n- `buildGuidance()`: skip `DOMAIN_KNOWLEDGE_GUIDANCE` text when disabled\n- `workspaceFilesNotice()`: select no-knowledge notice variant when disabled\n- `buildKnowledgeBlock()`: return empty string immediately when disabled\n\n## What is NOT affected when `disableKnowledgeContext()` is called\n\n- AGENTS.md injection\n- MEMORY.md injection\n- Memory tools (memory_search, memory_get, etc.)\n- Memory recall guidance\n- Session context (date, OS, workspace path)\n- All existing constructor signatures\n\n## Testing\n\n- All existing `WorkspaceContextMiddleware*Test` classes pass unchanged (6-arg constructor retained)\n- Suggested new test: `WorkspaceContextMiddlewareKnowledgePromptTest` mirroring the existing memory-prompt test, asserting `## Domain Knowledge` guidance, `KNOWLEDGE.md` body, `Knowledge files:` catalog, and notice text are all absent when disabled while `AGENTS.md` / `MEMORY.md` / `<memory_context>` remain present\n\n## Backward compatibility\n\n- No existing API changes\n- Default behavior unchanged (knowledge injection enabled)\n- All 6 existing constructor overloads work as before",
